{:mulog/duration 124042, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory", :grain/event-ids (#uuid "019e4322-4229-7067-8dee-e2a0659f1a81" #uuid "019e4322-4229-7068-ae76-6625a24a37b5" #uuid "019e4322-4227-70fb-a1c9-4ebe3f1ca726"), :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YsMrXnh-XDj6bS9h7JIzGRzydsgKo", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YsMrXnh-XDj6bS9h7JIzGRzydsgKo", :mulog/timestamp 1779242779177, :metric/name "GrainAppendEvents", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YsMs8nn-B85FyTgcClKB0MHJ2Sgzz", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory/append}
{:mulog/duration 2813416, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/command {:tick-id #uuid "5a6cf594-ae2d-4ace-9417-cc9bb8d80da9", :writes {:major-changes "1. **MAJOR (Legal/Financial): Elimination of Domestic Content Requirements.** \n   - Removal of Part 1 (B)(5)(iv), Section 4.4.4, and the entirety of Appendix C (Sections 1.1-1.7). Suppliers are no longer legally obligated to source a specific percentage of components or labor from Ontario.\n\n2. **MAJOR (Legal): Expansion of OPA Data Disclosure Authority.** \n   - Modification of Section 6.5. This grants the OPA broad authority to share facility data with government agencies under the umbrella of \"public health and safety\" and \"emergency planning.\"\n\n3. **MINOR (Clarification/Administrative): Mandatory \"Prescribed Form\" Usage.** \n   - Modifications to Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, and 9. All formal communications (contact changes, terminations, amendments) must now use specific OPA-provided templates.\n\n4. **MINOR (Clarification): OPA Discretionary Waivers for Re-contracting.** \n   - Modification to Appendix A (Project Eligibility Requirements (c)). Softens the prohibition on facilities that have previously reached commercial operation by allowing OPA written consent.\n\n5. **COSMETIC: Formatting and Pagination.** \n   - Adjustments in Part 1 (C) and Appendices D-1, D-2, and E.", :impact-analysis "1. **Elimination of Domestic Content (Impact: Supplier):** \n   - **Risk Shift:** Significant reduction in compliance risk and financial burden for the **Supplier**. Previously, failing to meet the 60% threshold (per the old Section 4.4.4) could constitutes a breach of representation. Removing this allows Suppliers to source cheaper international components (e.g., solar panels, inverters) without jeopardizing the contract.\n   - **Validation:** Reference removal of Appendix C Domestic Content Tables and Section 4.4.4.\n\n2. **Data Disclosure (Impact: Supplier/OPA):** \n   - **Risk Shift:** Shift in privacy risk toward the **Supplier**. The OPA gains protection against claims of confidentiality breach when sharing project data with emergency services or government ministries (Section 6.5). Suppliers lose some control over their facility's data privacy.\n   - **Validation:** Reference new additions to Section 6.5 regarding \"public health and safety.\"\n\n3. **Standardization via \"Prescribed Form\" (Impact: Supplier):** \n   - **Risk Shift:** Increase in administrative rigidity for the **Supplier**. Failure to use the exact version of a form found on the Website (as defined in Appendix A) could lead to the rejection of amendments or termination notices, potentially causing missed deadlines.\n   - **Validation:** Reference new definitions in Appendix A and requirements in Sections 8.1 and 9.\n\n4. **Eligibility Discretion (Impact: OPA):** \n   - **Risk Shift:** The **OPA** increases its \"sole and absolute discretion\" over project eligibility. While this provides a potential \"out\" for certain Suppliers to re-apply for contracts (Appendix A), it concentrates power in the OPA to act as a gatekeeper without objective criteria.\n   - **Validation:** Reference Appendix A \"Project Eligibility Requirements (c)\" and Appendix C \"Existing Building\" definitions."}, :command/name :sheet/complete-node-execution, :command/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:06:19.174928-05:00", :command/id #uuid "93d1b602-0f7f-40e0-b2b1-cd5280a4eb5a", :duration-ms 8144, :usage {:prompt-tokens 995, :completion-tokens 1471, :total-tokens 2466}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "82176ee3-956d-49ee-91c9-e7aa7761921d", :sheet-id #uuid "51930646-88b4-4b39-9b50-46560bef46c7"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YsMrXnh-XDj6bS9h7JIzGRzydsgKo", :mulog/timestamp 1779242779175, :metric/name "CommandProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YsMrXnh-XDj6bS9h7JIzGRzydsgKo", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/process-command, :metric/resolution :high}
