{:mulog/duration 9551042, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "5a6cf594-ae2d-4ace-9417-cc9bb8d80da9", :event/tags #{[:node #uuid "cd6ac7bd-b725-4835-99b0-c10b563df6a5"] [:sheet #uuid "51930646-88b4-4b39-9b50-46560bef46c7"] [:tick #uuid "5a6cf594-ae2d-4ace-9417-cc9bb8d80da9"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:06:19.182687-05:00", :inputs {:document-survey "### Structural Comparison: microFIT v2.0 vs. v3.1.1\n\n**1. Shared Sections (Present in Both Versions):**\n*   **Part 1 – Contract Details:** Sections A (Contract and Supplier Information), B (Facility Characteristics), and C (Documents Included).\n*   **Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions:**\n    1. Term\n    2. Pricing Provisions and Payment\n    3. Environmental Attributes\n    4. Representations and Warranties\n    5. Covenants\n    6. General Conditions\n    7. Notices\n    8. Termination\n    9. Amendment\n    10. Assignment\n    11. Governing Law\n    12. Dispute Resolution\n    13. LDC Failure to Pay\n    14. Suppliers Composed of Multiple Entities\n*   **All Appendices:** Appendix A (Definitions), B (Price Calculation), C (Solar PV), D-1 (Direct Connection), D-2 (Indirect Connection), and E (LDC Schedule) exist in both.\n\n**2. New Components / Significant Internal Additions in v3.1.1:**\n*   **Prescribed Forms:** Integration of \"Prescribed Form\" requirements for Supplier contact changes (5.1.2), Notices (7.2), termination (8.1), and amendments (9).\n*   **New Definitions (Appendix A):** \"Prescribed Form\" and \"Website\" (with URL) are new.\n*   **Data Disclosure:** Expansion of Section 6.5 \"Disclosure of Information\" to include emergency services and public officials for health and safety.\n\n**3. Removed Components in v3.1.1:**\n*   **Domestic Content grids:** Version 2.0 contained detailed \"Domestic Content Requirements\" and three \"Domestic Content Grids\" (Crystalline Silicon, Thin-Film, and Concentrated PV) in Appendix C. These have been entirely removed from the Version 3.1.1 Appendix C.\n*   **Domestic Content Warranty:** Section 4.4.4 of v2.0 (Representations and Warranties regarding Domestic Content) was removed in v3.1.1.", :section-diffs "The following is a section-by-section comparison identifying the changes between microFIT Contract Version 2.0 and Version 3.1.1.\n\n### **Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **B. FACILITY CHARACTERISTICS (5)(iv):** **Removed.** The \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" requirement (previously 60% for solar PV) has been removed from Part 1.\n*   **C. DOCUMENTS INCLUDED:** **No change** (Note: Formatting adjusted, but substance remains the same).\n\n### **Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **Section 4.4 (Necessary Rights and Compliance):**\n    *   **4.4.4:** **Removed.** The representation that a solar facility has a Domestic Content Level greater than or equal to the Minimum Required Domestic Content Level has been deleted. (Subsequent clauses renumbered).\n*   **Section 5.1 (Facility Characteristics):**\n    *   **5.1.2:** **Modified.** Added the requirement that notification of changes to contact information must be made in the \"Prescribed Form.\"\n*   **Section 6.5 (Collection/Disclosure of Information):**\n    *   **Collection:** **Modified.** Removed the reference to collecting information to \"establish compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level.\"\n    *   **Disclosure:** **Modified.** Removed \"compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" from the list of sharable information. \n    *   **Disclosure (Additions):** Added a new provision allowing OPA to disclose Facility details to government ministries/agencies \"for purposes of promoting public health and safety and allowing emergency services personnel... to plan and respond properly in the event of an emergency.\"\n*   **Section 7.2 (Change of Contact Information):** **Modified.** Added the requirement that notice of change must be in the \"Prescribed Form.\"\n*   **Section 8.1 (Termination on Notice):** **Modified.** Added the requirement that notice of termination must be in the \"Prescribed Form.\"\n*   **Section 9 (Amendment):** **Modified.** Added the requirement that amendments must be reduced to writing \"in the Prescribed Form.\"\n\n### **Appendix A – Definitions**\n*   **Domestic Content Level:** **Removed.**\n*   **Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** **Removed.**\n*   **Prescribed Form:** **Added.** New definition: \"means, in relation to a form, the latest version of the corresponding form appearing on the Website...\"\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements (c):** **Modified.** Added \"unless otherwise consented to by the OPA in writing in its sole and absolute discretion\" regarding facilities that have previously reached commercial operation.\n*   **Website:** **Added.** New definition: \"means the OPA’s Renewable Energy Feed-In Tariff Program website...\"\n\n### **Appendix C – Solar Photovoltaic Schedule**\n*   **Defined Terms (Existing Building):** **Modified.** Expanded to include buildings where the OPA \"in its sole and absolute discretion, issued a written confirmation that the building will be deemed an Existing Building.\"\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements (Sections 1.1 to 1.7 and Tables 1-3):** **Removed.** The entire regulatory framework for Domestic Content (Qualifying Percentages, Designated Activities, and Grids) has been deleted.\n\n### **Appendix D-1, D-2, and E**\n*   **No change.** (Note: Minor formatting/pagination differences only).", :major-changes "1. **MAJOR (Legal/Financial): Elimination of Domestic Content Requirements.** \n   - Removal of Part 1 (B)(5)(iv), Section 4.4.4, and the entirety of Appendix C (Sections 1.1-1.7). Suppliers are no longer legally obligated to source a specific percentage of components or labor from Ontario.\n\n2. **MAJOR (Legal): Expansion of OPA Data Disclosure Authority.** \n   - Modific